1
00:00:09,310 --> 00:00:10,580
(Lee Min Jung)

2
00:00:14,190 --> 00:00:15,420
(Kim Ji Seok)

3
00:00:21,960 --> 00:00:24,830
(OK! Let's Get Divorced)

4
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:26,330
(All child actor scenes were filmed with a guardian present...)

5
00:00:26,400 --> 00:00:27,800
(with professional staff and in accordance with safety guidelines.)

6
00:00:29,230 --> 00:00:30,770
The one who almost died that day...

7
00:00:32,800 --> 00:00:33,970
wasn't me.

8
00:00:35,510 --> 00:00:36,670
The one who got stabbed...

9
00:00:41,310 --> 00:00:42,310
was you.

10
00:00:44,150 --> 00:00:46,220
What are you talking about? I have to work. Get out.

11
00:00:48,920 --> 00:00:50,050
No, Mi Young, wait.

12
00:00:50,290 --> 00:00:51,490
No, wait...

13
00:01:06,740 --> 00:01:07,810
It wasn't you.

14
00:01:09,970 --> 00:01:10,980
It was me.

15
00:01:12,640 --> 00:01:13,650
I...

16
00:01:16,550 --> 00:01:18,720
was the one who put you in danger.

17
00:01:20,450 --> 00:01:21,450
I...

18
00:01:22,420 --> 00:01:24,460
I almost killed you.

19
00:01:26,620 --> 00:01:28,730
I'm sorry.

20
00:01:29,690 --> 00:01:30,700
I'm sorry.

21
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:33,000
I'm sorry.

22
00:01:36,070 --> 00:01:37,200
What do I...

23
00:01:39,740 --> 00:01:40,910
What do I do?

24
00:01:47,610 --> 00:01:48,650
Someone might see us.

25
00:01:49,180 --> 00:01:50,180
Get up.

26
00:02:00,290 --> 00:02:01,290
Let's go.

27
00:02:01,860 --> 00:02:03,190
People are waiting.

28
00:02:17,010 --> 00:02:19,210
(Senior Vow Renewal Event)

29
00:02:33,220 --> 00:02:36,390
Okay, everyone, on the count of three,

30
00:02:36,830 --> 00:02:38,660
say "cheese."

31
00:02:40,670 --> 00:02:42,470
One, two.

32
00:02:44,640 --> 00:02:47,070
Oh? CEO Baek.

33
00:02:48,870 --> 00:02:49,870
Are you okay?

34
00:02:50,740 --> 00:02:51,740
I'm fine.

35
00:02:53,610 --> 00:02:55,810
It looks like CEO Baek is moved.

36
00:02:55,980 --> 00:02:59,650
- You're making me teary-eyed. - Thank you, CEO Baek.

37
00:02:59,720 --> 00:03:01,420
- Please don't cry. - Don't cry.

38
00:03:01,420 --> 00:03:03,420
I'm sorry.

39
00:03:06,520 --> 00:03:09,130
All right, let's take it again.

40
00:03:11,160 --> 00:03:13,160
One, two, three.

41
00:03:13,600 --> 00:03:15,770
Cheese.

42
00:03:23,370 --> 00:03:24,580
Good job, everyone.

43
00:03:25,240 --> 00:03:26,640
- Good work. - Thank you.

44
00:03:26,880 --> 00:03:27,880
Vice President Kang.

45
00:03:28,780 --> 00:03:30,720
Did CEO Ji already leave for the day?

46
00:03:31,020 --> 00:03:32,320
He said he was tired and left early.

47
00:03:33,250 --> 00:03:34,250
That makes sense.

48
00:03:34,590 --> 00:03:36,920
He didn't have a moment's rest all day.

49
00:03:37,590 --> 00:03:38,690
What about CEO Baek?

50
00:03:39,220 --> 00:03:40,760
CEO Baek is still in her office.

51
00:03:41,230 --> 00:03:42,230
She said she still has work to finish.

52
00:03:42,790 --> 00:03:46,500
On a day like this, we should be throwing a huge company party.

53
00:03:48,300 --> 00:03:50,840
I seriously need to find a new job.

54
00:03:51,640 --> 00:03:52,800
Darn it.

55
00:03:53,070 --> 00:03:54,940
Darn it, this is no fun at all.

56
00:03:57,610 --> 00:03:59,640
Hey, Manager Song, wait up.

57
00:04:10,560 --> 00:04:12,260
I want to die.

58
00:04:12,490 --> 00:04:13,760
I said don't.

59
00:04:37,080 --> 00:04:38,220
No, Mi Young, wait.

60
00:04:38,220 --> 00:04:39,380
No, wait.

61
00:04:39,380 --> 00:04:40,990
Mi Young, just wait.

62
00:05:32,840 --> 00:05:34,440
What are you doing here?

63
00:05:36,140 --> 00:05:37,840
Don't tell me you left your house again.

64
00:05:38,640 --> 00:05:40,310
Have a drink with me.

65
00:05:45,180 --> 00:05:47,950
I don't normally drink during work hours,

66
00:05:49,590 --> 00:05:51,220
but let's just say we're off the clock today.

67
00:05:54,590 --> 00:05:56,160
Thank you, Lawyer Jeon.

68
00:05:57,860 --> 00:05:59,230
Since we're off the clock,

69
00:05:59,900 --> 00:06:02,370
let's drop the formalities too.

70
00:06:03,740 --> 00:06:04,740
Cheers.

71
00:06:13,810 --> 00:06:14,850
The ratio is killer, isn't it?

72
00:06:15,580 --> 00:06:16,580
Yes.

73
00:06:17,010 --> 00:06:19,750
I'm practically a national champion when it comes to making somaek.

74
00:06:20,350 --> 00:06:22,950
Even somaek needs that sentimental touch in its ratio.

75
00:06:31,900 --> 00:06:32,900
So...

76
00:06:34,630 --> 00:06:36,600
are you ready to tell me now...

77
00:06:38,470 --> 00:06:40,170
about what happened today?

78
00:06:43,740 --> 00:06:44,740
Today...

79
00:06:48,350 --> 00:06:50,520
I found out something shocking.

80
00:06:53,080 --> 00:06:54,090
I...

81
00:06:59,720 --> 00:07:01,460
stabbed my husband.

82
00:07:03,090 --> 00:07:04,100
You stabbed him?

83
00:07:06,730 --> 00:07:07,800
Three years ago,

84
00:07:08,330 --> 00:07:11,870
I told you that my husband had assaulted me.

85
00:07:15,070 --> 00:07:16,070
Well...

86
00:07:18,610 --> 00:07:20,440
That wasn't true.

87
00:07:23,580 --> 00:07:24,580
That day,

88
00:07:26,520 --> 00:07:29,220
I was the one who hurt my husband.

89
00:07:33,620 --> 00:07:36,730
My husband didn't abandon me and run away.

90
00:07:40,000 --> 00:07:43,470
He ran out to save his own life.

91
00:07:52,410 --> 00:07:54,310
I completely lost it that day.

92
00:07:57,880 --> 00:07:58,920
I stabbed...

93
00:08:02,920 --> 00:08:04,320
my husband with a knife.

94
00:08:09,260 --> 00:08:11,260
He was the one who got hurt.

95
00:08:14,130 --> 00:08:17,170
How must he have felt being blamed all this time?

96
00:08:19,170 --> 00:08:20,640
And why did he...

97
00:08:23,410 --> 00:08:25,040
keep taking it all...

98
00:08:25,980 --> 00:08:28,050
and hiding the truth until now?

99
00:08:30,280 --> 00:08:31,280
And...

100
00:08:33,950 --> 00:08:34,950
why did I think...

101
00:08:35,920 --> 00:08:38,460
I knew everything about my husband?

102
00:08:40,590 --> 00:08:41,960
Maybe that's why...

103
00:08:43,930 --> 00:08:45,560
you've ended up here.

104
00:08:49,630 --> 00:08:53,440
Then, starting now, let's use the lawsuit...

105
00:08:54,640 --> 00:08:56,140
to get to know him properly, one thing at a time.

106
00:08:58,180 --> 00:09:00,580
Whether our goal becomes an amicable divorce...

107
00:09:01,750 --> 00:09:03,650
or a dramatic reconciliation...

108
00:09:05,150 --> 00:09:07,490
is something we can decide after you truly get to know...

109
00:09:07,490 --> 00:09:08,620
your husband.

110
00:09:25,940 --> 00:09:26,940
Seung Ho.

111
00:09:28,210 --> 00:09:30,580
Are you hiding anything from me?

112
00:09:31,280 --> 00:09:33,410
What? What's this all of a sudden?

113
00:09:33,840 --> 00:09:35,480
Oh, come on, you know.

114
00:09:35,610 --> 00:09:37,950
Something you can't easily open up about,

115
00:09:39,080 --> 00:09:41,420
even with family.

116
00:09:42,420 --> 00:09:43,750
A secret shame of your own?

117
00:09:44,760 --> 00:09:45,760
I don't know.

118
00:09:47,690 --> 00:09:50,230
- Crypto? - Gosh, forget it.

119
00:09:51,130 --> 00:09:52,730
Why? Did your wife find out?

120
00:09:53,230 --> 00:09:54,300
Is that why you came running here?

121
00:09:56,330 --> 00:10:00,200
I guess there are no real secrets in this world.

122
00:10:01,210 --> 00:10:02,910
Why did we have to run into each other then?

123
00:10:04,010 --> 00:10:05,480
In times like that, you just pretend you don't know.

124
00:10:08,150 --> 00:10:09,180
Pretend I don't know?

125
00:10:09,610 --> 00:10:11,180
The thing about life is...

126
00:10:11,850 --> 00:10:13,820
if you keep pretending you don't know and ignore it,

127
00:10:14,220 --> 00:10:15,890
it will eventually become insignificant.

128
00:10:16,950 --> 00:10:18,620
If you go on with life and completely ignore it,

129
00:10:19,160 --> 00:10:21,390
you'll just think, "Oh, right. That happened."

130
00:10:22,330 --> 00:10:23,730
"That time with crypto,"

131
00:10:25,430 --> 00:10:27,500
"I lost all my money."

132
00:10:28,430 --> 00:10:29,770
It's that kind of moment...

133
00:10:30,940 --> 00:10:32,700
of enlightenment that they say will come.

134
00:10:57,500 --> 00:10:58,560
Won Ho, you're back?

135
00:11:01,500 --> 00:11:03,300
- Yes. - Hey,

136
00:11:04,470 --> 00:11:05,540
would you like some black tea?

137
00:11:21,320 --> 00:11:22,350
Try it.

138
00:11:22,950 --> 00:11:23,990
It smells wonderful.

139
00:11:40,670 --> 00:11:42,540
I have something to tell you.

140
00:11:43,710 --> 00:11:45,280
Okay, go ahead.

141
00:11:47,110 --> 00:11:49,450
Can you just pretend you don't know?

142
00:11:51,120 --> 00:11:52,120
What?

143
00:11:53,850 --> 00:11:56,420
What you heard from Father Kwon today and...

144
00:11:57,220 --> 00:11:58,860
everything you saw today.

145
00:12:02,390 --> 00:12:04,660
Just pretend you didn't see or hear any of it.

146
00:12:07,130 --> 00:12:10,100
Why should I do that?

147
00:12:11,000 --> 00:12:13,070
Because it's been a long time.

148
00:12:17,880 --> 00:12:19,680
It really doesn't bother me anymore.

149
00:12:19,780 --> 00:12:22,750
I'm fine, so you don't have to worry about it.

150
00:12:25,180 --> 00:12:26,180
All right.

151
00:12:26,820 --> 00:12:29,120
Then I will.

152
00:12:31,120 --> 00:12:32,120
Okay.

153
00:12:54,040 --> 00:12:55,180
(Father Kwon)

154
00:12:56,750 --> 00:12:57,750
Yes, Father.

155
00:12:57,820 --> 00:12:59,450
I'm surprised to get a call from you.

156
00:13:01,450 --> 00:13:02,450
Pardon?

157
00:13:04,290 --> 00:13:07,220
The vow renewal volunteer service we talked about?

158
00:13:08,190 --> 00:13:09,260
The thing is,

159
00:13:09,560 --> 00:13:12,000
it's not really something I can decide on my own.

160
00:13:15,270 --> 00:13:16,270
Really?

161
00:13:17,700 --> 00:13:19,140
Did Mi Young really say that?

162
00:13:21,510 --> 00:13:23,270
Do you think this is natural?

163
00:13:23,940 --> 00:13:24,940
What is?

164
00:13:25,580 --> 00:13:26,980
You said it yourself yesterday...

165
00:13:27,040 --> 00:13:29,010
that doing volunteer work right now makes no sense.

166
00:13:29,210 --> 00:13:30,810
You even called me hopeless.

167
00:13:31,020 --> 00:13:32,380
And whenever Father Kwon is mentioned,

168
00:13:32,450 --> 00:13:33,580
you can't stand him.

169
00:13:33,650 --> 00:13:35,750
Now you suddenly decide overnight that you're going to do it?

170
00:13:35,820 --> 00:13:37,420
And you even called him yourself?

171
00:13:38,790 --> 00:13:41,130
Well, why not?

172
00:13:41,830 --> 00:13:44,700
I thought about it, and it seems like a good cause.

173
00:13:44,960 --> 00:13:46,260
Let's just do it, honey.

174
00:13:46,730 --> 00:13:48,400
"Let's just do it, honey?"

175
00:13:48,830 --> 00:13:50,870
Why? You don't want to?

176
00:13:53,770 --> 00:13:56,270
Look, we made an agreement yesterday, right?

177
00:13:56,540 --> 00:13:58,480
To act like yesterday never happened.

178
00:13:58,780 --> 00:14:00,280
Yes, so?

179
00:14:00,910 --> 00:14:02,210
No, what I mean is...

180
00:14:04,010 --> 00:14:06,120
Try to be more natural!

181
00:14:06,180 --> 00:14:08,050
Why are you suddenly acting so unlike yourself?

182
00:14:10,550 --> 00:14:11,590
I'm warning you.

183
00:14:12,020 --> 00:14:14,120
If you're unnatural, you get a yellow card.

184
00:14:17,730 --> 00:14:19,000
That face gets you two.

185
00:14:22,270 --> 00:14:23,330
Darn it.

186
00:14:24,870 --> 00:14:25,940
Honey.

187
00:14:29,770 --> 00:14:30,910
Darn it, that's hot.

188
00:14:31,180 --> 00:14:33,940
Oh my, are you okay? Did you burn yourself?

189
00:14:34,450 --> 00:14:38,150
- Be careful. Give it to me. - No, I'm fine.

190
00:14:48,630 --> 00:14:50,030
We have five design proposals...

191
00:14:50,030 --> 00:14:51,430
for the bride, Kim Jin Kyeong, right?

192
00:14:51,630 --> 00:14:54,030
- Which did we narrow it down to? - This one and these.

193
00:14:54,100 --> 00:14:55,900
- These three? - Yes.

194
00:15:07,040 --> 00:15:08,250
What were they?

195
00:15:11,220 --> 00:15:12,480
What's with you two?

196
00:15:15,050 --> 00:15:16,050
Your wife.

197
00:15:16,620 --> 00:15:18,020
Why is she suddenly acting like that toward you?

198
00:15:19,760 --> 00:15:22,360
Is that part of her lawsuit strategy?

199
00:15:23,760 --> 00:15:24,760
Lawsuit strategy?

200
00:15:24,900 --> 00:15:26,460
To make you so uncomfortable...

201
00:15:26,700 --> 00:15:28,270
that you'll just give her the divorce, or something?

202
00:15:29,430 --> 00:15:30,730
Hey, you felt it too, right?

203
00:15:30,970 --> 00:15:32,170
Even just watching from the sidelines,

204
00:15:32,240 --> 00:15:33,670
it's incredibly awkward, isn't it?

205
00:15:33,770 --> 00:15:35,310
It's more than just awkward.

206
00:15:35,370 --> 00:15:36,810
She's like a completely different person.

207
00:15:38,910 --> 00:15:41,180
At this point, shouldn't we do some digging on her?

208
00:15:41,850 --> 00:15:43,880
Like maybe she took out a loan against your house or something.

209
00:15:45,380 --> 00:15:46,650
No, it's not like that.

210
00:15:47,250 --> 00:15:48,290
Then what is it?

211
00:15:48,820 --> 00:15:50,890
There really is something going on between you two, isn't there?

212
00:15:52,320 --> 00:15:53,490
I don't know.

213
00:15:56,560 --> 00:15:58,900
This is really becoming a problem.

214
00:16:05,700 --> 00:16:08,010
I was so impressed.

215
00:16:08,470 --> 00:16:10,610
How can you be so nice to Won Ho?

216
00:16:12,780 --> 00:16:14,510
Did it look that way to you too?

217
00:16:14,750 --> 00:16:17,050
Yes. He might just pack his bags and leave.

218
00:16:19,220 --> 00:16:22,850
You're being so uncomfortably nice to him...

219
00:16:22,950 --> 00:16:24,920
to make Won Ho leave on his own accord,

220
00:16:25,620 --> 00:16:26,720
is that it?

221
00:16:27,390 --> 00:16:28,930
Anyway, CEO Baek,

222
00:16:28,990 --> 00:16:30,860
you are so brilliant.

223
00:16:31,100 --> 00:16:34,300
How do I usually treat Ji Won Ho, then?

224
00:16:34,530 --> 00:16:35,630
Are you kidding?

225
00:16:35,770 --> 00:16:37,670
You treated him worse than dirt.

226
00:16:37,800 --> 00:16:40,240
Sometimes you'd treat Won Ho like he was invisible,

227
00:16:40,300 --> 00:16:41,940
not speaking to him or answering him.

228
00:16:42,470 --> 00:16:44,070
Was I really that bad?

229
00:16:44,270 --> 00:16:47,610
The person involved is always the last to know.

230
00:16:48,110 --> 00:16:50,350
Anyway, just keep it up a little longer.

231
00:16:50,710 --> 00:16:53,750
I bet Won Ho will be out of the house before the weekend.

232
00:16:54,120 --> 00:16:55,450
I bet 50 cents on it.

233
00:16:59,090 --> 00:17:02,360
Excuse me, Young Min. Is the thing I asked for earlier ready?

234
00:17:16,770 --> 00:17:18,640
I figured you'd be here already.

235
00:17:19,280 --> 00:17:20,940
How did you know I was here?

236
00:17:21,110 --> 00:17:22,310
Are you spying on me?

237
00:17:22,380 --> 00:17:23,450
Am I allowed to?

238
00:17:24,520 --> 00:17:26,720
I'm not in the mood for jokes right now.

239
00:17:27,380 --> 00:17:30,390
Why? Is something wrong?

240
00:17:30,750 --> 00:17:32,560
It's none of your business.

241
00:17:33,290 --> 00:17:34,320
Come on.

242
00:17:34,860 --> 00:17:36,860
But I tell you everything about me.

243
00:17:37,130 --> 00:17:39,200
That's my point. Why would you trust me?

244
00:17:39,630 --> 00:17:40,960
If you keep trusting people that easily,

245
00:17:41,030 --> 00:17:42,200
you're going to ruin your life.

246
00:17:44,700 --> 00:17:48,740
If I'm going to ruin it, I want to ruin it with you.

247
00:17:50,740 --> 00:17:52,840
I told you not to cross the line, didn't I?

248
00:17:55,750 --> 00:17:57,080
Are you going home today?

249
00:17:58,380 --> 00:17:59,480
Why do you ask?

250
00:18:01,750 --> 00:18:03,890
Don't go home.

251
00:18:04,150 --> 00:18:08,260
Just hang out with me. Let's get hammered.

252
00:18:08,360 --> 00:18:10,190
No way. Who knows what trouble we'd get into.

253
00:18:10,390 --> 00:18:12,300
I'm never getting wasted with you again.

254
00:18:13,000 --> 00:18:14,000
What?

255
00:18:14,160 --> 00:18:16,030
You're not planning on going home today,

256
00:18:16,370 --> 00:18:17,370
right?

257
00:18:18,940 --> 00:18:19,970
Why don't you just...

258
00:18:20,270 --> 00:18:22,110
never go home again?

259
00:18:22,310 --> 00:18:24,580
Stop talking nonsense. Just drink up and go.

260
00:18:24,640 --> 00:18:25,640
Darn it.

261
00:18:50,470 --> 00:18:52,700
I haven't had enough to drink yet.

262
00:18:53,940 --> 00:18:57,640
Can we go inside and have just one more drink?

263
00:18:57,840 --> 00:18:59,540
There you go again, asking for trouble.

264
00:18:59,610 --> 00:19:01,850
Hurry and go. You'll miss the last bus.

265
00:19:02,280 --> 00:19:03,410
You really want me to go?

266
00:19:04,210 --> 00:19:05,280
Go, already.

267
00:19:05,550 --> 00:19:07,180
If you keep this up, I'll seriously...

268
00:19:07,320 --> 00:19:09,420
- Seriously. - won't hang out with you anymore.

269
00:19:11,820 --> 00:19:13,220
Look at that face.

270
00:19:13,990 --> 00:19:15,360
It's so cute.

271
00:19:16,660 --> 00:19:18,700
What? You always laugh at the weirdest things.

272
00:19:19,160 --> 00:19:20,200
Hurry up and go.

273
00:19:20,500 --> 00:19:21,500
Okay.

274
00:19:22,170 --> 00:19:23,170
Sleep well.

275
00:19:27,040 --> 00:19:29,040
(Jihwaja Motel)

276
00:19:29,810 --> 00:19:31,110
I told you to go.

277
00:19:31,340 --> 00:19:32,340
Okay.

278
00:19:50,030 --> 00:19:51,030
What the...

279
00:19:53,730 --> 00:19:56,130
Why do you keep coming here? Why aren't you sleeping at home?

280
00:19:56,800 --> 00:19:59,400
Let's go. Hurry. I made dinner at home.

281
00:20:00,070 --> 00:20:01,670
Seriously, what's going on?

282
00:20:02,470 --> 00:20:04,880
Since when have you ever worried about me like this?

283
00:20:05,440 --> 00:20:08,980
You don't care where I pass out or what I eat.

284
00:20:11,680 --> 00:20:14,080
Just act like you normally do, please.

285
00:20:15,090 --> 00:20:16,490
It's not like I'm asking you to be nice to me.

286
00:20:16,550 --> 00:20:20,120
Just go your way, and I'll go mine. Just let me live in peace.

287
00:20:20,190 --> 00:20:22,290
Why are you making such a fuss and bothering me?

288
00:20:23,360 --> 00:20:24,490
Won Ho.

289
00:20:24,490 --> 00:20:27,160
It's harder for me when you act like this.

290
00:20:29,600 --> 00:20:32,570
It makes me uncomfortable. It makes you uncomfortable too.

291
00:20:32,770 --> 00:20:33,770
It's just...

292
00:20:34,140 --> 00:20:36,810
Life becomes uncomfortable.

293
00:20:39,310 --> 00:20:41,040
So just leave me alone, will you?

294
00:20:44,050 --> 00:20:45,080
All right.

295
00:20:46,620 --> 00:20:47,750
I'll go then.

296
00:20:48,690 --> 00:20:49,690
But...

297
00:20:51,220 --> 00:20:52,220
I want you to know...

298
00:20:53,220 --> 00:20:55,830
it's not that I didn't ask because I didn't care.

299
00:20:57,290 --> 00:21:00,700
I may not have been nice to you or ever really showed it.

300
00:21:03,830 --> 00:21:05,540
But I was always worried.

301
00:21:07,840 --> 00:21:08,910
The truth is,

302
00:21:10,910 --> 00:21:13,410
I've always been concerned about you.

303
00:21:47,880 --> 00:21:48,910
Hello.

304
00:22:17,410 --> 00:22:20,280
(Jihwaja Motel)

305
00:22:52,140 --> 00:22:55,550
Mi Young. Did you see the supermoon tonight?

306
00:23:09,830 --> 00:23:11,060
To think...

307
00:23:11,330 --> 00:23:13,400
I'm drinking with you on the night of a supermoon.

308
00:23:14,200 --> 00:23:15,730
My prayers to the moon were answered.

309
00:23:18,540 --> 00:23:21,100
Thank you. If it wasn't for you,

310
00:23:21,840 --> 00:23:23,670
I wouldn't have even known there was a moon out.

311
00:23:26,080 --> 00:23:28,610
Are you really okay?

312
00:23:31,350 --> 00:23:33,580
You don't look well.

313
00:23:34,280 --> 00:23:36,750
Why? Do I look that bad?

314
00:23:37,520 --> 00:23:39,320
No, that's not what I meant.

315
00:23:47,630 --> 00:23:48,730
I think my husband...

316
00:23:50,700 --> 00:23:52,470
is dating Hee Ju.

317
00:23:54,340 --> 00:23:55,340
What?

318
00:23:56,270 --> 00:23:59,380
I just went to the motel to get my husband,

319
00:24:00,580 --> 00:24:02,410
and Hee Ju was in the hallway.

320
00:24:04,450 --> 00:24:07,320
He blew up when he saw me,

321
00:24:09,250 --> 00:24:11,020
and I think it must have been because of Hee Ju.

322
00:24:22,430 --> 00:24:24,530
I thought I knew everything.

323
00:24:26,940 --> 00:24:29,010
I even thought I was okay with it.

324
00:24:34,110 --> 00:24:35,380
But now that it's actually happening,

325
00:24:36,410 --> 00:24:37,550
it feels strange.

326
00:24:41,720 --> 00:24:42,920
Hey, Mi Young.

327
00:24:45,020 --> 00:24:46,020
If by any chance...

328
00:24:47,360 --> 00:24:49,930
- If you're having a hard time... - No.

329
00:24:50,360 --> 00:24:53,000
I'm not having a hard time. Let's just drink.

330
00:25:14,150 --> 00:25:15,650
You have to nip this in the bud.

331
00:25:16,090 --> 00:25:18,860
So you're saying he slept here last night too?

332
00:25:18,920 --> 00:25:20,960
Mi Young came to get him, but he still stayed the night.

333
00:25:21,020 --> 00:25:22,290
He sent her home alone.

334
00:25:22,360 --> 00:25:23,930
That mindless fool...

335
00:25:23,990 --> 00:25:25,500
Hey, pack up every single thing here,

336
00:25:25,500 --> 00:25:27,130
down to his last pair of underwear.

337
00:25:27,230 --> 00:25:29,670
Let's clean this whole place out so he can never come back.

338
00:25:29,670 --> 00:25:30,830
Yes, ma'am.

339
00:25:37,070 --> 00:25:39,710
- Wait. This isn't his. - What's with these clothes?

340
00:26:00,930 --> 00:26:02,070
Just a second...

341
00:26:03,070 --> 00:26:04,830
Wait, hold on...

342
00:26:23,290 --> 00:26:24,390
(Open the door.)

343
00:26:35,070 --> 00:26:36,570
Hello? Is anyone here?

344
00:27:15,340 --> 00:27:16,840
She was very pretty.

345
00:27:52,780 --> 00:27:53,780
Oh my.

346
00:27:55,750 --> 00:27:57,950
- Who are you? - And who might you be,

347
00:27:58,010 --> 00:28:00,280
letting yourself into an empty house?

348
00:28:03,390 --> 00:28:04,390
Hey, Won Ho.

349
00:28:05,090 --> 00:28:06,090
What?

350
00:28:06,560 --> 00:28:08,890
Were you the one running... Oh, you are.

351
00:28:09,090 --> 00:28:11,760
Mom, she's the young woman I was telling you about,

352
00:28:11,900 --> 00:28:13,300
the one who came to the motel with Won Ho.

353
00:28:13,430 --> 00:28:14,530
What?

354
00:28:15,230 --> 00:28:16,300
Who are you?

355
00:28:16,770 --> 00:28:17,900
I'm...

356
00:28:18,570 --> 00:28:20,240
I'm CEO Ji's girlfriend.

357
00:28:20,700 --> 00:28:22,240
So you're saying that you're...

358
00:28:22,410 --> 00:28:25,140
my son, Ji Won Ho's, girlfriend?

359
00:28:26,610 --> 00:28:28,850
So you must be CEO Ji's mother.

360
00:28:29,150 --> 00:28:30,450
Hello. My name is...

361
00:28:30,510 --> 00:28:31,610
Ahn Hee Ju.

362
00:28:31,680 --> 00:28:35,090
Hold on. You seem to be very confused.

363
00:28:35,350 --> 00:28:38,760
My son is already married.

364
00:28:38,760 --> 00:28:39,990
I know.

365
00:28:40,360 --> 00:28:42,990
- You know? - Yes. I'm well aware.

366
00:28:43,390 --> 00:28:46,400
Miss, I think it'd be best for you to leave now.

367
00:28:46,530 --> 00:28:48,100
You know he's married?

368
00:28:48,200 --> 00:28:50,700
Are you trying to break up a home?

369
00:28:50,970 --> 00:28:52,000
No way.

370
00:28:52,440 --> 00:28:54,840
CEO Ji's marriage fell apart ages ago.

371
00:28:55,410 --> 00:28:57,510
Don't tell me you didn't know.

372
00:28:57,710 --> 00:29:00,310
What? What did you just say?

373
00:29:00,380 --> 00:29:02,310
- What crap are you spouting now? - Mom, wait...

374
00:29:02,310 --> 00:29:03,380
You need to get out of here...

375
00:29:03,450 --> 00:29:04,450
- Let go of me. - Mom!

376
00:29:06,120 --> 00:29:07,150
Come here!

377
00:29:14,060 --> 00:29:15,490
I've thought about it,

378
00:29:16,360 --> 00:29:17,960
and rather than going on like this,

379
00:29:18,430 --> 00:29:20,330
I think it's best we end things quickly.

380
00:29:21,900 --> 00:29:24,700
We need to finalize the divorce...

381
00:29:24,700 --> 00:29:26,540
and sort out our lives.

382
00:29:26,540 --> 00:29:28,070
It will be a relief for everyone.

383
00:29:28,540 --> 00:29:29,940
Hee Ju included.

384
00:29:31,010 --> 00:29:32,010
Hee Ju?

385
00:29:32,910 --> 00:29:35,210
Hee Ju? Why are you bringing her up?

386
00:29:37,380 --> 00:29:38,750
Don't play dumb.

387
00:29:39,420 --> 00:29:41,750
I already know everything.

388
00:29:41,990 --> 00:29:44,450
That you two have been going in and out of motels.

389
00:29:44,750 --> 00:29:47,620
Oh, come on.

390
00:29:48,060 --> 00:29:50,260
I'm sick of making excuses.

391
00:29:50,330 --> 00:29:52,900
I told you it's not like that. It really isn't.

392
00:29:53,730 --> 00:29:57,100
And I know what you're misunderstanding about her,

393
00:29:57,170 --> 00:29:58,940
but it's because she's just different from others...

394
00:29:59,000 --> 00:30:00,000
How do I put this...

395
00:30:00,070 --> 00:30:02,110
She's special in her own way.

396
00:30:02,470 --> 00:30:04,710
What? Special?

397
00:30:04,970 --> 00:30:06,210
Yes.

398
00:30:09,080 --> 00:30:10,280
Why are you looking at me like that?

399
00:30:12,380 --> 00:30:13,620
- Let go of me! - Mom!

400
00:30:13,680 --> 00:30:15,650
- I said, let go. - Let go of me!

401
00:30:15,720 --> 00:30:17,120
- Let go of me! - Let go of her hair.

402
00:30:17,720 --> 00:30:20,760
- Let go. Miss. You let go first. - You let go first.

403
00:30:21,490 --> 00:30:23,330
- Mom. Stop it. - Why you...

404
00:30:23,330 --> 00:30:24,330
Let go!

405
00:30:27,100 --> 00:30:28,900
What? Girlfriend?

406
00:30:28,970 --> 00:30:30,530
Who is this crazy tramp?

407
00:30:30,600 --> 00:30:33,600
That's right, I'm his girlfriend!

408
00:30:33,600 --> 00:30:34,970
What did you say?

409
00:30:35,410 --> 00:30:36,410
That hurts!

410
00:30:37,210 --> 00:30:39,140
- That's nonsense! - I'm his girlfriend!

411
00:30:45,010 --> 00:30:46,520
Oh, my hair.

412
00:30:47,050 --> 00:30:48,350
Why you...

413
00:30:49,520 --> 00:30:52,060
How dare a brat like you act so bold?

414
00:30:52,820 --> 00:30:54,820
This lady is completely hopeless.

415
00:30:54,820 --> 00:30:57,090
- Do you have any idea who I am? - I don't, you tramp.

416
00:30:57,090 --> 00:30:58,900
Do I look like I need to know who you are?

417
00:30:59,000 --> 00:31:01,200
Where did Won Ho pick up such a leech?

418
00:31:01,260 --> 00:31:03,270
Both of you, just stop it. Come on, Mom.

419
00:31:03,470 --> 00:31:06,040
You. I'm not done with you.

420
00:31:06,500 --> 00:31:09,040
You're the one who's going to regret this.

421
00:31:10,340 --> 00:31:11,340
Hello?

422
00:31:11,710 --> 00:31:13,440
There's a crazy woman here. A psycho.

423
00:31:13,980 --> 00:31:15,280
Hello?

424
00:31:16,450 --> 00:31:18,680
So "special" people, when they drink and get sleepy,

425
00:31:18,820 --> 00:31:21,280
can just lie down and sleep wherever they want?

426
00:31:21,350 --> 00:31:24,520
Anyone can see she's not "special." She's weird.

427
00:31:24,620 --> 00:31:27,660
She's just weird and brazen. She's just too strange.

428
00:31:27,720 --> 00:31:29,930
I told you she's not. She's really a good person.

429
00:31:29,990 --> 00:31:32,700
She's just a little different from most people, that's all.

430
00:31:32,760 --> 00:31:34,260
What? A good person?

431
00:31:34,400 --> 00:31:35,430
What, special?

432
00:31:35,500 --> 00:31:36,500
Hey, you're unbelievable...

433
00:31:36,570 --> 00:31:38,370
No, when I said she's special, I meant...

434
00:31:38,430 --> 00:31:40,940
that she's just a bit different from other people her age.

435
00:31:40,940 --> 00:31:43,170
That's it. You'll see if you get to know her.

436
00:31:43,240 --> 00:31:45,710
I'm telling you, she's not like anyone else.

437
00:31:46,210 --> 00:31:48,140
You just won't give it up.

438
00:31:48,440 --> 00:31:49,450
What is wrong with you?

439
00:31:49,510 --> 00:31:51,010
How can you be so stubborn in the middle of all this?

440
00:31:51,150 --> 00:31:53,020
Hey, whether she's special or one of a kind,

441
00:31:53,080 --> 00:31:55,450
is that something you'd defend with your life?

442
00:31:55,520 --> 00:31:58,660
When did I ever say I'd defend her with my life?

443
00:31:58,790 --> 00:32:01,290
Then why do you keep nitpicking over something so small?

444
00:32:01,360 --> 00:32:02,460
What did I say about her?

445
00:32:02,530 --> 00:32:03,960
Did I call her pretty? What did I say?

446
00:32:04,030 --> 00:32:05,730
All I did was say one thing, that she was special,

447
00:32:05,800 --> 00:32:07,630
so why are you so fixated on it and making such a scene?

448
00:32:07,760 --> 00:32:10,600
Look at him, still insisting that she's special.

449
00:32:10,670 --> 00:32:12,000
Hey, nitpicking?

450
00:32:12,070 --> 00:32:14,900
- You're such a stubborn leech. - Yes, I'm a stubborn leech.

451
00:32:14,900 --> 00:32:16,410
But you're just pigheaded.

452
00:32:16,470 --> 00:32:18,340
Hey, you're the one who's stubborn for no reason, you jerk.

453
00:32:18,410 --> 00:32:19,540
Right back at you. Times a million.

454
00:32:19,610 --> 00:32:21,640
So childish. Unbelievably childish, really.

455
00:32:21,710 --> 00:32:23,180
You're the childish one.

456
00:32:23,250 --> 00:32:24,880
- Looks like they're finally... - You better watch your mouth!

457
00:32:24,880 --> 00:32:26,080
back to normal.

458
00:32:26,220 --> 00:32:30,220
It's awkward to watch, but why do I feel so relieved?

459
00:32:31,350 --> 00:32:33,390
I was so scared, my legs were shaking.

460
00:32:33,420 --> 00:32:35,390
- I'm so scared. - I'm not kidding.

461
00:32:35,390 --> 00:32:38,030
- Hey. Stop it. Okay? - Hey, Seung Ho.

462
00:32:41,160 --> 00:32:42,630
What? The police station?

463
00:32:44,700 --> 00:32:47,600
Wait, why Mi Young? Why does she have to come too?

464
00:32:50,410 --> 00:32:52,440
- Please calm down. - I'm so pissed off, darn it.

465
00:32:56,750 --> 00:32:58,310
This is my actual sister-in-law.

466
00:32:58,880 --> 00:32:59,920
This one is the fake one.

467
00:33:00,620 --> 00:33:01,920
Detective, if you were in her shoes,

468
00:33:02,090 --> 00:33:03,990
and a complete stranger popped out of your son's house...

469
00:33:04,120 --> 00:33:05,290
and pretended to be his wife,

470
00:33:05,360 --> 00:33:06,590
wouldn't you be shocked?

471
00:33:06,660 --> 00:33:09,430
When I think about how shocked I was earlier...

472
00:33:09,760 --> 00:33:11,960
- Oh, my heart. - I was just...

473
00:33:12,030 --> 00:33:14,900
going to get something CEO Ji needed,

474
00:33:14,960 --> 00:33:17,370
but this woman just grabbed my hair out of nowhere.

475
00:33:17,430 --> 00:33:20,140
But that's no reason to call the police right away.

476
00:33:20,200 --> 00:33:22,410
And to be frank, miss, you didn't just stand there either.

477
00:33:22,470 --> 00:33:25,710
Oh, what a life. What did I do in a past life...

478
00:33:25,780 --> 00:33:27,340
to deserve such humiliation?

479
00:33:27,410 --> 00:33:29,450
This is so unfair, I can't take it. I just can't.

480
00:33:29,510 --> 00:33:31,410
I should just bite my tongue and die. I really should.

481
00:33:31,480 --> 00:33:33,920
Mom, come on. Don't say that.

482
00:33:34,320 --> 00:33:37,520
Hey. Does seeing this mess mean nothing to you?

483
00:33:37,990 --> 00:33:41,190
- Pardon? - If you'd held your rightful place,

484
00:33:41,260 --> 00:33:42,960
do you think any of this would have happened?

485
00:33:43,160 --> 00:33:44,190
It's because you insisted on divorce...

486
00:33:44,260 --> 00:33:46,100
and turned the whole family upside down...

487
00:33:46,230 --> 00:33:49,130
that some crazy woman latched onto our Won Ho!

488
00:33:49,200 --> 00:33:50,430
Mom, that's enough.

489
00:33:50,500 --> 00:33:52,840
Are you having trouble understanding me, ma'am?

490
00:33:53,000 --> 00:33:54,800
CEO Ji's sham of a marriage ended a long time ago.

491
00:33:54,870 --> 00:33:56,170
I already told you that.

492
00:33:56,240 --> 00:33:57,670
I can't believe this crazy tramp.

493
00:33:57,740 --> 00:33:59,240
Will you shut your mouth?

494
00:33:59,340 --> 00:34:00,580
- I'll shut that mouth of yours... - Let go of me.

495
00:34:00,640 --> 00:34:01,640
- Mom. - Mom...

496
00:34:02,010 --> 00:34:03,610
- How dare she! - Mom, let go of her.

497
00:34:03,680 --> 00:34:04,880
- My hair. - Let go!

498
00:34:06,650 --> 00:34:08,480
Calm down!

499
00:34:12,260 --> 00:34:13,960
How did you know the passcode to the house?

500
00:34:15,930 --> 00:34:17,390
Is she really your girlfriend?

501
00:34:19,230 --> 00:34:22,200
- What? - I said she wasn't.

502
00:34:22,500 --> 00:34:24,700
Hey, Won Ho, tell him. She's not, right?

503
00:34:24,870 --> 00:34:28,040
- Well... - I am CEO Ji's girlfriend.

504
00:34:28,100 --> 00:34:30,170
What is with this psycho? Seriously.

505
00:34:30,240 --> 00:34:31,740
Seriously, a joke can only go so far.

506
00:34:31,840 --> 00:34:33,580
Miss, you're going to end up in jail for this.

507
00:34:33,580 --> 00:34:34,610
Hey, Won Ho.

508
00:34:34,680 --> 00:34:35,810
Why are you just standing there, you punk?

509
00:34:35,880 --> 00:34:37,050
Sir, please tell me now,

510
00:34:37,210 --> 00:34:38,550
or should I just charge her with trespassing?

511
00:34:38,610 --> 00:34:42,620
Hurry up. I'm your girlfriend, right?

512
00:34:42,690 --> 00:34:45,690
Hey. Do you think my son is crazy to date a girl like you?

513
00:34:45,760 --> 00:34:47,260
That's right. I am crazy.

514
00:34:48,620 --> 00:34:49,630
Won Ho.

515
00:34:52,530 --> 00:34:53,560
Is that true?

516
00:34:55,030 --> 00:34:56,030
Yes,

517
00:34:56,470 --> 00:34:57,600
I am...

518
00:34:58,200 --> 00:34:59,570
Ahn Hee Ju's...

519
00:35:01,740 --> 00:35:03,110
boyfriend.

520
00:35:15,420 --> 00:35:18,420
Hey, do you believe this? She's his girlfriend?

521
00:35:18,490 --> 00:35:20,090
I'll acknowledge it over my dead body.

522
00:35:20,160 --> 00:35:22,360
That freaking psycho!

523
00:35:23,060 --> 00:35:24,590
Wait, just listen to me before you go.

524
00:35:25,190 --> 00:35:27,860
You have to at least let me explain what happened.

525
00:35:27,860 --> 00:35:29,570
Let go. I don't want to hear it.

526
00:35:29,630 --> 00:35:30,870
Fine, I'll admit it.

527
00:35:30,870 --> 00:35:33,200
Just as you said, Hee Ju isn't just a weird girl.

528
00:35:33,200 --> 00:35:34,400
She's a complete psycho.

529
00:35:34,500 --> 00:35:36,640
But I can't throw her in jail for that.

530
00:35:36,640 --> 00:35:39,140
You saw my mom, didn't you? If I hadn't defended like that...

531
00:35:39,710 --> 00:35:41,080
Did she break down the door?

532
00:35:41,440 --> 00:35:44,350
- What? - You two must be quite serious.

533
00:35:44,410 --> 00:35:47,720
- It's not like that, really. - Let's just end this already.

534
00:35:48,080 --> 00:35:49,690
Mi Young, wait...

535
00:35:54,720 --> 00:35:56,490
Darn it.

536
00:36:05,900 --> 00:36:07,940
(Yeonnam Police Station)

537
00:36:08,200 --> 00:36:09,440
CEO Ji.

538
00:36:11,210 --> 00:36:12,210
Hey!

539
00:36:12,880 --> 00:36:15,980
I'm sorry. Please forgive me.

540
00:36:18,920 --> 00:36:20,150
Why you...

541
00:36:30,330 --> 00:36:31,830
You, tell me.

542
00:36:32,260 --> 00:36:34,630
What were you thinking?

543
00:36:36,570 --> 00:36:37,770
I'm sorry.

544
00:36:39,200 --> 00:36:40,840
The other day, by chance,

545
00:36:40,900 --> 00:36:43,470
I happened to see you putting in your passcode,

546
00:36:43,710 --> 00:36:44,970
and out of curiosity...

547
00:36:46,180 --> 00:36:47,410
I must have been crazy.

548
00:36:47,640 --> 00:36:49,350
I was so wrong.

549
00:36:49,410 --> 00:36:51,580
Fine. Let's put that aside.

550
00:36:51,810 --> 00:36:53,950
But what about the girlfriend part?

551
00:36:54,050 --> 00:36:56,090
If I didn't say that,

552
00:36:56,750 --> 00:36:58,490
I was afraid I'd look like a weirdo...

553
00:36:58,550 --> 00:37:02,460
You're already way past weird. You're a complete lunatic. Got it?

554
00:37:07,330 --> 00:37:08,630
Crying isn't going to work.

555
00:37:09,400 --> 00:37:10,900
I'm never seeing you again.

556
00:37:16,170 --> 00:37:18,240
Let go of me while I'm still being nice.

557
00:37:18,940 --> 00:37:19,940
Please.

558
00:37:20,340 --> 00:37:21,740
Please, don't be mad.

559
00:37:22,380 --> 00:37:24,950
You're the one who needs to stop. Let's just stop.

560
00:37:26,780 --> 00:37:28,020
Then use me.

561
00:37:31,190 --> 00:37:32,190
What?

562
00:37:32,520 --> 00:37:35,360
I heard you and your wife talking.

563
00:37:35,560 --> 00:37:37,390
You really want to end things now, don't you?

564
00:37:38,630 --> 00:37:40,800
But you're struggling because it isn't working out.

565
00:37:41,200 --> 00:37:44,100
- What does that have to do with... - Since it's come to this anyway...

566
00:37:47,540 --> 00:37:48,870
Just use me.

567
00:37:50,340 --> 00:37:51,710
It's how I can survive,

568
00:37:53,280 --> 00:37:54,940
and it's how you can survive too.

569
00:37:57,680 --> 00:37:58,950
I'll help you.

570
00:38:17,700 --> 00:38:19,440
I spoke with Father Kwon,

571
00:38:20,100 --> 00:38:21,670
and he thinks that for now, instead of a vow renewal,

572
00:38:21,740 --> 00:38:24,340
a wedding for multicultural brides would be a better idea.

573
00:38:25,010 --> 00:38:26,610
The organization Father Kwon works with...

574
00:38:26,680 --> 00:38:28,340
has a lot more multicultural members,

575
00:38:29,110 --> 00:38:31,610
and creating dresses for various races, nationalities,

576
00:38:31,610 --> 00:38:32,850
and body types...

577
00:38:33,720 --> 00:38:35,850
would be a great experience for us too.

578
00:38:36,790 --> 00:38:38,050
Fine, do that then.

579
00:38:40,520 --> 00:38:42,630
Are you really okay with this?

580
00:38:43,060 --> 00:38:44,360
Why are you asking me?

581
00:38:44,360 --> 00:38:46,560
You can discuss that with your girlfriend now.

582
00:38:46,930 --> 00:38:49,000
- What? - Are you done?

583
00:38:49,400 --> 00:38:50,600
I'm leaving now.

584
00:38:52,440 --> 00:38:53,970
I need to ask you for something.

585
00:38:59,580 --> 00:39:01,540
I need you to sign a written pledge.

586
00:39:02,680 --> 00:39:03,680
A written pledge?

587
00:39:04,280 --> 00:39:05,280
Yes.

588
00:39:06,120 --> 00:39:07,520
That even if Hee Ju and I see each other,

589
00:39:07,650 --> 00:39:10,520
you won't raise any objections in the future.

590
00:39:16,860 --> 00:39:18,090
Is that for real?

591
00:39:18,530 --> 00:39:21,660
Well, it's not like I have time to make things up.

592
00:39:21,860 --> 00:39:22,870
My gosh.

593
00:39:23,930 --> 00:39:26,340
- I mean, how could he... - I know.

594
00:39:26,340 --> 00:39:29,340
But seriously, why is CEO Ji acting like this?

595
00:39:29,870 --> 00:39:30,870
I know.

596
00:39:31,710 --> 00:39:32,810
Maybe the stress from the divorce lawsuit...

597
00:39:32,880 --> 00:39:33,880
was too much for him?

598
00:39:34,040 --> 00:39:36,050
The divorce isn't even finalized yet,

599
00:39:36,110 --> 00:39:37,510
but he's already dating...

600
00:39:39,420 --> 00:39:43,150
And CEO Baek, didn't you agree to it too easily?

601
00:39:43,990 --> 00:39:45,490
Without even talking to your lawyer?

602
00:39:45,860 --> 00:39:48,120
He asked so matter-of-factly...

603
00:39:48,190 --> 00:39:50,630
that I didn't even have a chance to think or respond.

604
00:39:50,860 --> 00:39:54,600
Gosh, between CEO Ji demanding something like that...

605
00:39:55,260 --> 00:39:58,200
and CEO Baek just agreeing to it,

606
00:39:58,970 --> 00:40:01,540
you're both really something else.

607
00:40:02,000 --> 00:40:03,010
Unbelievable.

608
00:40:03,440 --> 00:40:07,980
But what is it about that woman that has CEO Ji so captivated?

609
00:40:08,480 --> 00:40:09,480
Is it because she's pretty?

610
00:40:10,980 --> 00:40:12,950
Or because she's young?

611
00:40:13,720 --> 00:40:15,790
Oh, honestly.

612
00:40:17,320 --> 00:40:21,020
Anyway, are you really okay, CEO Baek?

613
00:40:21,520 --> 00:40:23,730
Yes. Why wouldn't I be okay?

614
00:40:24,430 --> 00:40:25,590
We're getting a divorce anyway.

615
00:40:28,530 --> 00:40:31,000
Hey, think before you speak.

616
00:40:39,110 --> 00:40:41,480
You did great.

617
00:40:42,140 --> 00:40:44,080
For once, you made a rational decision...

618
00:40:44,080 --> 00:40:45,150
and handled things well.

619
00:40:45,210 --> 00:40:48,720
This is the first time I'm ever going to praise you.

620
00:40:49,020 --> 00:40:51,220
You did great.

621
00:40:53,090 --> 00:40:55,090
Why are you being so formal all of a sudden?

622
00:40:55,260 --> 00:40:57,030
I have to be.

623
00:40:57,430 --> 00:40:58,660
In the middle of a divorce lawsuit,

624
00:40:59,060 --> 00:41:01,730
it's not enough that you're dating someone 12 years younger,

625
00:41:01,860 --> 00:41:03,570
but you even got a written pledge.

626
00:41:04,070 --> 00:41:06,000
As someone who's still single,

627
00:41:06,170 --> 00:41:08,200
you're a legend in my book.

628
00:41:09,540 --> 00:41:11,210
Oh, come on. Stop it.

629
00:41:12,470 --> 00:41:14,510
That written pledge is useless.

630
00:41:16,050 --> 00:41:18,980
- Pardon? - I told you not to play with fire.

631
00:41:19,050 --> 00:41:22,080
And now you're openly dating after getting a written pledge?

632
00:41:22,150 --> 00:41:23,450
Are you out of your mind?

633
00:41:23,920 --> 00:41:25,720
What did your wife even write in that pledge?

634
00:41:26,090 --> 00:41:28,620
That you, her husband, can date another woman,

635
00:41:28,690 --> 00:41:29,890
and she won't try to mess up the lawsuit?

636
00:41:29,960 --> 00:41:30,960
Something like that?

637
00:41:31,160 --> 00:41:33,030
Yes, something like that.

638
00:41:33,330 --> 00:41:35,800
I don't know how Mi Soon ended up with a son like you.

639
00:41:37,470 --> 00:41:40,070
So, am I not allowed to date during the divorce lawsuit?

640
00:41:40,140 --> 00:41:41,840
Does that violate my right to the pursuit of happiness?

641
00:41:42,240 --> 00:41:43,240
It does.

642
00:41:43,710 --> 00:41:46,180
By all means, keep pursuing your happiness.

643
00:41:46,440 --> 00:41:47,740
Knock yourself out.

644
00:41:52,080 --> 00:41:53,780
Hey, do we have any soju?

645
00:41:54,720 --> 00:41:56,820
- Should I get you some? - Bring it over.

646
00:41:58,150 --> 00:41:59,150
The big bottle.

647
00:42:07,630 --> 00:42:09,730
It's totally official now.

648
00:42:10,370 --> 00:42:11,370
What?

649
00:42:11,700 --> 00:42:13,840
I got a written pledge from CEO Baek.

650
00:42:14,300 --> 00:42:15,740
A pledge that says even if I date CEO Ji,

651
00:42:15,910 --> 00:42:17,770
she won't cause any trouble.

652
00:42:18,940 --> 00:42:20,940
She wrote what? A written pledge?

653
00:42:21,410 --> 00:42:22,750
I told you before, didn't I?

654
00:42:23,210 --> 00:42:25,080
That you have to fight for love.

655
00:42:25,550 --> 00:42:28,250
So you're here to brag about...

656
00:42:28,880 --> 00:42:30,050
how you won your prize?

657
00:42:30,390 --> 00:42:32,890
Honestly, isn't this great news for you, too?

658
00:42:35,490 --> 00:42:36,490
Great news?

659
00:42:37,790 --> 00:42:38,830
Well, this is awkward.

660
00:42:39,900 --> 00:42:43,800
I'm afraid I have some bad news for you, Hee Ju.

661
00:42:54,080 --> 00:42:57,410
Hey, is what your wife said true?

662
00:42:58,010 --> 00:42:59,010
What?

663
00:42:59,680 --> 00:43:02,320
You and that woman, Ahn Hee Ju...

664
00:43:03,020 --> 00:43:04,190
Oh, that...

665
00:43:04,750 --> 00:43:06,890
- Then, yes. - Are you out of your mind?

666
00:43:07,420 --> 00:43:09,490
How could you do this during the lawsuit?

667
00:43:09,790 --> 00:43:12,590
It just happened that way.

668
00:43:13,200 --> 00:43:15,660
Hey, be honest. There's something else, isn't there?

669
00:43:16,630 --> 00:43:19,230
Is she blackmailing you with something she has on you?

670
00:43:19,870 --> 00:43:21,170
Hey, how did you know?

671
00:43:22,140 --> 00:43:23,140
For real?

672
00:43:23,540 --> 00:43:25,040
Of course not, you idiot. I'm kidding.

673
00:43:25,980 --> 00:43:28,210
Do you really think I'd let some kid intimidate me?

674
00:43:39,760 --> 00:43:40,760
Where are you going?

675
00:43:42,020 --> 00:43:43,130
To see that kid.

676
00:44:07,650 --> 00:44:08,650
What?

677
00:44:09,280 --> 00:44:10,350
Unbelievable.

678
00:44:14,020 --> 00:44:15,120
Vice President Kang?

679
00:44:17,460 --> 00:44:18,860
Manager Song.

680
00:44:19,460 --> 00:44:22,400
Is something wrong?

681
00:44:22,930 --> 00:44:25,730
I'm just fuming.

682
00:44:26,500 --> 00:44:27,500
Fuming?

683
00:44:29,000 --> 00:44:30,010
Manager Song,

684
00:44:30,570 --> 00:44:33,180
do you know anything about Ahn Hee Ju?

685
00:44:34,010 --> 00:44:35,040
Ahn Hee Ju?

686
00:44:38,710 --> 00:44:41,620
CEO Ji's new girlfriend?

687
00:44:41,720 --> 00:44:43,320
Don't give me that "girlfriend" nonsense.

688
00:44:43,690 --> 00:44:46,590
You scared me. Why are you yelling?

689
00:44:49,790 --> 00:44:51,890
Manager Song, don't go around...

690
00:44:52,630 --> 00:44:54,030
saying things like that so carelessly.

691
00:44:54,730 --> 00:44:55,730
What?

692
00:45:00,470 --> 00:45:01,770
Goodness.

693
00:45:05,040 --> 00:45:06,110
What's with him?

694
00:45:14,020 --> 00:45:15,980
Everyone's going to think I'm crazy.

695
00:45:19,190 --> 00:45:21,390
Getting a written pledge during a lawsuit just to date someone.

696
00:45:22,760 --> 00:45:23,930
Especially with someone like you.

697
00:45:24,260 --> 00:45:25,630
What's wrong with someone like me?

698
00:45:27,860 --> 00:45:30,800
Are we sure this is okay to do? Is this the best way?

699
00:45:31,200 --> 00:45:33,100
This way, you can get a clean break.

700
00:45:33,770 --> 00:45:36,740
I'm sure that by now, your wife's feelings...

701
00:45:37,210 --> 00:45:38,970
are plummeting.

702
00:45:39,610 --> 00:45:41,080
Her affection for you is just gone.

703
00:45:42,810 --> 00:45:45,880
By the way, you haven't told anyone...

704
00:45:46,550 --> 00:45:48,320
about us pretending to date, right?

705
00:45:49,950 --> 00:45:51,050
Right.

706
00:45:51,520 --> 00:45:52,550
Okay.

707
00:45:53,420 --> 00:45:55,090
Confidentiality is key for something like this.

708
00:45:55,660 --> 00:45:57,530
You sound like a secret agent.

709
00:45:59,030 --> 00:46:01,630
Oh, right. I got fired.

710
00:46:02,760 --> 00:46:06,570
- What? - I was fired by Calvin.

711
00:46:07,400 --> 00:46:09,540
What? Why? Why'd you suddenly get fired?

712
00:46:10,010 --> 00:46:11,140
I'm not sure.

713
00:46:11,740 --> 00:46:14,710
It's probably either jealousy or revenge.

714
00:46:15,280 --> 00:46:16,280
What are you talking about?

715
00:46:16,510 --> 00:46:18,850
"How dare you get into a relationship before I do?"

716
00:46:19,310 --> 00:46:20,320
That's the jealousy.

717
00:46:21,050 --> 00:46:23,250
"For making my woman uncomfortable."

718
00:46:24,420 --> 00:46:25,420
That's the revenge.

719
00:46:25,990 --> 00:46:29,220
What? "Making my woman uncomfortable"?

720
00:46:29,560 --> 00:46:31,260
Of course she'd be uncomfortable.

721
00:46:31,790 --> 00:46:34,600
The thought of CEO Baek stewing because of me...

722
00:46:35,560 --> 00:46:38,770
is probably enough to tick Calvin off.

723
00:46:43,170 --> 00:46:44,340
CEO Ji.

724
00:46:45,910 --> 00:46:47,810
Can't you help me out?

725
00:46:48,640 --> 00:46:49,650
Help you with what?

726
00:46:49,880 --> 00:46:51,780
Are you just going to leave me like this?

727
00:46:52,650 --> 00:46:55,680
As a victim of Calvin's revenge?

728
00:47:01,560 --> 00:47:02,860
This dish has cilantro in it.

729
00:47:03,230 --> 00:47:05,530
- Yes. - Can I get one without cilantro?

730
00:47:05,860 --> 00:47:06,860
Yes.

731
00:47:10,470 --> 00:47:11,670
Mi Young, you don't eat cilantro.

732
00:47:13,740 --> 00:47:15,140
You remembered.

733
00:47:16,040 --> 00:47:17,410
Here, let's eat.

734
00:47:21,280 --> 00:47:23,310
I heard you fired Hee Ju.

735
00:47:25,480 --> 00:47:30,090
Was it because of me? Because you thought I'd be upset?

736
00:47:30,620 --> 00:47:34,260
No. She deserved to be fired.

737
00:47:35,790 --> 00:47:38,860
If you really did do it because of me,

738
00:47:39,190 --> 00:47:40,300
it was a complete failure.

739
00:47:41,900 --> 00:47:44,770
As of today, Hee Ju is working at our company.

740
00:47:45,370 --> 00:47:48,500
She got fast-tracked thanks to my husband's pull.

741
00:47:54,040 --> 00:47:56,580
Hey, I'm fine. Don't look at me like that.

742
00:47:59,250 --> 00:48:00,250
Mi Young.

743
00:48:06,290 --> 00:48:07,290
This is delicious.

744
00:48:08,020 --> 00:48:09,320
This place is really good.

745
00:48:14,200 --> 00:48:15,960
- Start wrapping up and head inside. - Okay.

746
00:48:15,960 --> 00:48:16,970
All right.

747
00:48:18,630 --> 00:48:19,640
Ji Won Ho.

748
00:48:25,710 --> 00:48:26,780
Darn it.

749
00:48:33,150 --> 00:48:35,650
Seeing you camped out here waiting for me,

750
00:48:35,920 --> 00:48:37,320
you must have a lot of free time these days.

751
00:48:37,750 --> 00:48:40,820
I almost did, but things are getting more complicated.

752
00:48:41,420 --> 00:48:42,420
Because of you.

753
00:48:42,620 --> 00:48:44,730
- What? - I'll get straight to the point.

754
00:48:45,360 --> 00:48:47,860
Fire Ahn Hee Ju.

755
00:48:50,700 --> 00:48:51,700
Why should I?

756
00:48:52,300 --> 00:48:53,800
Why would I do that?

757
00:48:54,200 --> 00:48:57,970
Then why, out of all the photographers,

758
00:48:58,710 --> 00:49:00,280
did you have to hire Ahn Hee Ju?

759
00:49:05,850 --> 00:49:08,850
You didn't think about Mi Young at all, did you?

760
00:49:09,550 --> 00:49:12,620
- What? - When people make decisions,

761
00:49:13,420 --> 00:49:14,620
there's such a thing as common courtesy.

762
00:49:15,820 --> 00:49:18,330
I don't care what you decide to do,

763
00:49:19,090 --> 00:49:22,100
but your lack of courtesy is really rubbing me the wrong way.

764
00:49:23,130 --> 00:49:24,430
So, you showing up unannounced...

765
00:49:24,500 --> 00:49:26,940
and telling me whether or not to fire my employee,

766
00:49:27,570 --> 00:49:28,740
is that what you call courteous?

767
00:49:30,840 --> 00:49:33,680
I'll handle my own employees, so stay out of it.

768
00:49:34,210 --> 00:49:37,650
I find this kind of confrontation extremely unpleasant.

769
00:49:57,070 --> 00:49:59,770
Who was in this room...

770
00:50:06,410 --> 00:50:08,380
When you work hard and win a case,

771
00:50:08,580 --> 00:50:11,250
the payoff is pretty good.

772
00:50:14,180 --> 00:50:15,280
Gosh.

773
00:50:15,950 --> 00:50:17,620
She's surprisingly cute.

774
00:50:18,790 --> 00:50:19,860
Did something good happen?

775
00:50:20,320 --> 00:50:21,320
Gosh, you scared me.

776
00:50:21,790 --> 00:50:22,860
When did you get here?

777
00:50:25,060 --> 00:50:26,400
Got a minute to talk?

778
00:50:36,610 --> 00:50:37,670
It wasn't you.

779
00:50:40,910 --> 00:50:41,910
It was me.

780
00:50:43,710 --> 00:50:45,810
I was the one who put you in danger.

781
00:50:47,450 --> 00:50:48,450
I...

782
00:50:49,320 --> 00:50:51,390
I almost killed you.

783
00:50:53,620 --> 00:50:54,620
Someone might see us.

784
00:50:55,160 --> 00:50:56,160
Get up.

785
00:51:10,040 --> 00:51:11,140
I think my husband...

786
00:51:11,670 --> 00:51:13,410
is dating Hee Ju.

787
00:51:16,110 --> 00:51:19,110
I just went to the motel to get my husband,

788
00:51:20,280 --> 00:51:22,120
and Hee Ju was in the hallway.

789
00:51:24,590 --> 00:51:27,460
He blew up when he saw me,

790
00:51:29,360 --> 00:51:31,030
and I think it must have been because of Hee Ju.

791
00:51:49,080 --> 00:51:52,010
As of today, Hee Ju is working at our company.

792
00:51:52,450 --> 00:51:53,580
Thanks to my husband's pull.

793
00:51:53,920 --> 00:51:56,750
I'll handle my own employees, so stay out of it.

794
00:51:57,250 --> 00:52:00,720
I find this kind of confrontation extremely unpleasant.

795
00:52:03,260 --> 00:52:04,660
I told you before, didn't I?

796
00:52:05,330 --> 00:52:07,260
That you have to fight for love.

797
00:52:17,670 --> 00:52:18,670
What?

798
00:52:18,910 --> 00:52:20,940
Wait, you signed a written pledge about dating that girl?

799
00:52:21,110 --> 00:52:22,610
Are you out of your mind?

800
00:52:22,840 --> 00:52:25,650
Look, I told you. We both agreed to it.

801
00:52:25,710 --> 00:52:27,080
It's not because I actually like her.

802
00:52:27,280 --> 00:52:28,880
That's even weirder, man.

803
00:52:29,080 --> 00:52:31,350
If you genuinely liked the woman,

804
00:52:31,590 --> 00:52:32,850
then I could at least understand.

805
00:52:33,660 --> 00:52:35,320
But with a woman you don't even have feelings for...

806
00:52:37,260 --> 00:52:39,030
Hey, what do you think Mi Young will think?

807
00:52:39,430 --> 00:52:41,900
Well, she'll think I'm crazy.

808
00:52:42,600 --> 00:52:44,530
Dating someone in the middle of all this,

809
00:52:44,600 --> 00:52:45,830
like some woman-crazed lunatic.

810
00:52:46,100 --> 00:52:47,300
And you did it anyway, knowing that?

811
00:52:50,640 --> 00:52:52,140
I'm just going to be the bad guy, Seung Ho.

812
00:52:54,280 --> 00:52:56,310
I need Mi Young to think I'm a complete psycho...

813
00:52:57,210 --> 00:52:59,010
and that I'm someone she never wants to see again.

814
00:52:59,080 --> 00:53:00,580
That's the only way this will really be over.

815
00:53:03,790 --> 00:53:04,950
You're not confident, are you?

816
00:53:06,960 --> 00:53:08,790
The truth is, you're the one who's wavering.

817
00:53:09,420 --> 00:53:10,590
Your heart...

818
00:53:11,290 --> 00:53:13,230
can't let Mi Young go, right?

819
00:53:15,430 --> 00:53:16,430
Hey, Won Ho.

820
00:53:17,330 --> 00:53:20,570
Can't you just talk to Mi Young again and work things out?

821
00:53:22,240 --> 00:53:24,510
I'm saying this because I feel so bad for you.

822
00:53:24,570 --> 00:53:26,740
- Even now, go to Mi Young... - It's too late.

823
00:53:30,950 --> 00:53:32,550
For that to happen, Mi Young and I...

824
00:53:35,280 --> 00:53:36,720
I think we've come too far.

825
00:54:27,070 --> 00:54:28,070
Okay.

826
00:54:30,440 --> 00:54:31,440
Yes.

827
00:54:35,880 --> 00:54:38,280
Have you decided on a location for your wedding photos?

828
00:54:38,750 --> 00:54:41,380
We have a location in mind,

829
00:54:41,450 --> 00:54:43,020
but because of the nature of the location,

830
00:54:43,650 --> 00:54:45,920
it's a little hard finding a photographer.

831
00:54:47,990 --> 00:54:49,660
What's the location?

832
00:54:49,890 --> 00:54:50,890
- A cliff. - It's a cliff.

833
00:54:51,060 --> 00:54:52,990
We met while hiking on a cliff.

834
00:54:53,530 --> 00:54:55,230
And our first kiss also happened to be...

835
00:54:55,900 --> 00:54:56,900
- on the cliff. - On the cliff.

836
00:54:57,200 --> 00:54:58,830
Oh, a cliff.

837
00:55:00,100 --> 00:55:02,300
But if we can't find a photographer who agrees,

838
00:55:02,370 --> 00:55:03,370
we'll just have to scrap the idea.

839
00:55:03,640 --> 00:55:06,010
I hate this, really.

840
00:55:06,140 --> 00:55:07,310
Don't worry, baby.

841
00:55:09,680 --> 00:55:10,950
I'll do it.

842
00:55:22,290 --> 00:55:24,090
That place is too dangerous.

843
00:55:24,390 --> 00:55:26,960
But you have a photographer standing right here,

844
00:55:27,130 --> 00:55:28,130
and you're saying you don't have one?

845
00:55:28,360 --> 00:55:30,870
Hey, they said they want to shoot on a cliff.

846
00:55:31,000 --> 00:55:32,730
I'm telling you right now...

847
00:55:33,000 --> 00:55:35,600
that I'll do the cliff wedding shoot.

848
00:55:36,340 --> 00:55:37,770
Do you not know what a cliff is?

849
00:55:38,010 --> 00:55:40,740
It's a cliff, not some neighborhood hill.

850
00:55:41,240 --> 00:55:42,740
Does the location really matter?

851
00:55:44,150 --> 00:55:47,220
It doesn't matter. Because I'm a complete professional.

852
00:55:47,480 --> 00:55:49,420
Are you seriously doing this just to prove a point?

853
00:55:49,720 --> 00:55:51,290
Just trust me.

854
00:55:51,850 --> 00:55:54,690
I promise I'll make it back in one piece.

855
00:56:01,160 --> 00:56:04,030
There's a place over here with an amazing view of the cliff.

856
00:56:04,100 --> 00:56:06,300
- So beautiful. - Really?

857
00:56:08,100 --> 00:56:09,400
Please follow me carefully.

858
00:56:09,470 --> 00:56:10,910
- Okay. - Careful, darling.

859
00:56:10,910 --> 00:56:11,940
Okay.

860
00:56:11,940 --> 00:56:13,370
Oh, this is so beautiful.

861
00:56:13,880 --> 00:56:16,910
One, two, three. That's lovely.

862
00:56:17,780 --> 00:56:19,480
- Another pose. - Yes.

863
00:56:19,550 --> 00:56:22,320
Okay. One, two, three.

864
00:56:23,280 --> 00:56:25,990
Three. Two, three, and hold.

865
00:56:27,060 --> 00:56:28,060
Just a moment.

866
00:56:35,660 --> 00:56:38,430
- Ready. - Okay, let's keep going. It's fine.

867
00:56:38,500 --> 00:56:39,670
Great.

868
00:56:40,270 --> 00:56:41,270
Are you crazy?

869
00:56:41,700 --> 00:56:43,970
What? A cliff? Not just a mountain, but a cliff?

870
00:56:44,240 --> 00:56:46,810
I didn't force her. Hee Ju volunteered to do it.

871
00:56:46,880 --> 00:56:49,810
She wouldn't have gone if you hadn't brought it up!

872
00:56:50,080 --> 00:56:53,010
I know you're upset with me, but isn't this a bit much?

873
00:56:53,180 --> 00:56:54,650
Is that what you really think?

874
00:56:55,320 --> 00:56:57,390
If you weren't confident, you shouldn't have signed the pledge.

875
00:56:57,650 --> 00:56:58,890
Hey, Ji Won Ho.

876
00:57:00,320 --> 00:57:02,390
Big smiles, please.

877
00:57:03,560 --> 00:57:04,990
You look so beautiful.

878
00:57:05,160 --> 00:57:06,930
Oh, you're the best.

879
00:57:07,830 --> 00:57:09,460
Gorgeous. One more time.

880
00:57:09,800 --> 00:57:11,230
- Okay. - Here we go.

881
00:57:11,300 --> 00:57:12,300
Cheese.

882
00:57:12,730 --> 00:57:13,840
Smile.

883
00:57:17,540 --> 00:57:18,540
What?

884
00:57:20,940 --> 00:57:22,410
We should wrap things up now.

885
00:57:22,710 --> 00:57:24,950
I'll pack up, so you can head out first.

886
00:57:25,010 --> 00:57:26,880
Okay, break time, okay.

887
00:57:26,950 --> 00:57:29,850
Honey, it's so cold.

888
00:57:36,660 --> 00:57:37,660
Gosh...

889
00:57:44,800 --> 00:57:46,130
Hee Ju, are you okay?

890
00:57:46,730 --> 00:57:48,040
What? You're hurt?

891
00:57:49,140 --> 00:57:51,310
Okay, I'm on my way.

892
00:58:06,290 --> 00:58:07,290
Hey! What is this?

893
00:58:07,360 --> 00:58:08,360
What's going on?

894
00:58:08,720 --> 00:58:10,360
Hey, wait, hold on.

895
00:58:10,430 --> 00:58:12,290
Let me go! Help!

896
00:58:21,340 --> 00:58:22,970
The person you are calling is not answering...

897
00:58:43,420 --> 00:58:46,060
- Hey, excuse me! - Be quiet.

898
00:58:46,130 --> 00:58:47,130
- Hey. - Stay still.

899
00:58:47,530 --> 00:58:48,960
- Hey. - Shut your mouth.

900
00:58:49,030 --> 00:58:50,700
- Hey. - Calm down.

901
00:58:51,100 --> 00:58:52,370
Let's go quietly.

902
00:59:10,490 --> 00:59:12,020
- What is this? - Be quiet.

903
00:59:12,090 --> 00:59:14,160
Hey, who are you guys? Why are you doing this...

904
00:59:15,060 --> 00:59:16,160
Hee Ju...

905
00:59:17,290 --> 00:59:18,430
Hee Ju...

906
00:59:25,430 --> 00:59:27,200
Just trust me.

907
00:59:27,770 --> 00:59:30,770
I promise I'll make it back in one piece.

908
00:59:34,910 --> 00:59:36,280
- Stay still. - Hey!

909
00:59:36,340 --> 00:59:38,280
- Hey, you punk. - Darn it.

910
00:59:38,280 --> 00:59:40,420
- Hey, darn it. - Hey, you bastard.

911
00:59:41,350 --> 00:59:42,650
- Hey! - Shut up!

912
00:59:42,720 --> 00:59:43,720
Darn it!

913
00:59:43,990 --> 00:59:46,590
- Let go of me. - Hee Ju!

914
01:00:11,950 --> 01:00:13,350
- I'm not getting out! - Get out.

915
01:00:13,410 --> 01:00:14,680
- I'm not getting out, you bastards. - Get out!

916
01:00:15,420 --> 01:00:16,850
- Hey. - Get over here.

917
01:00:16,950 --> 01:00:18,650
- Come on. - Who are you? Let go of me.

918
01:00:19,220 --> 01:00:21,490
Who are you guys? You've got the wrong person.

919
01:00:22,960 --> 01:00:25,230
Where am I? Who are you people?

920
01:00:25,830 --> 01:00:27,060
Hee Ju!

921
01:00:32,630 --> 01:00:33,630
What?

922
01:00:44,650 --> 01:00:47,320
Hee Ju!

923
01:00:49,450 --> 01:00:52,950
Hee Ju!

924
01:01:03,430 --> 01:01:04,430
What do you think you're doing now?

925
01:01:08,740 --> 01:01:10,470
You... Calvin...

926
01:01:12,010 --> 01:01:13,510
What do you think you're doing?

927
01:01:14,310 --> 01:01:15,980
I didn't want it to come to this.

928
01:01:16,740 --> 01:01:17,750
You haven't forgotten...

929
01:01:18,350 --> 01:01:19,350
the promise, have you?

930
01:01:19,850 --> 01:01:22,150
- Promise? - You remember.

931
01:01:23,450 --> 01:01:24,450
Seven years ago,

932
01:01:25,190 --> 01:01:26,320
the promise we made.

933
01:01:28,560 --> 01:01:29,560
I...

934
01:01:29,960 --> 01:01:31,060
My Mi Young.

935
01:01:31,260 --> 01:01:32,960
Of course I'm going to make her happy.

936
01:01:33,430 --> 01:01:36,760
I will never hurt Mi Young the way you did.

937
01:01:37,830 --> 01:01:40,670
I'll make her so happy that she won't even remember...

938
01:01:40,670 --> 01:01:42,240
her time with you. I'll make sure of it.

939
01:01:47,980 --> 01:01:48,980
Well, then...

940
01:01:50,850 --> 01:01:51,850
Let's go fulfill...

941
01:01:53,210 --> 01:01:54,220
that promise.

942
01:02:16,000 --> 01:02:18,970
(OK! Let's Get Divorced)

943
01:02:20,270 --> 01:02:22,110
- It's Calvin. - What?

944
01:02:22,940 --> 01:02:26,680
If I had really wanted to, he would be dead.

945
01:02:27,150 --> 01:02:29,820
Let's just forget about the written pledge too.

946
01:02:29,880 --> 01:02:31,620
Just because of what Calvin said?

947
01:02:33,390 --> 01:02:34,620
CEO Baek,

948
01:02:35,160 --> 01:02:36,590
what is all this?

949
01:02:37,490 --> 01:02:39,090
Seriously, why are you being like this?

950
01:02:39,530 --> 01:02:42,300
It's not like Hee Ju went to that dangerous cliff again.

951
01:02:42,360 --> 01:02:44,230
This could be even more dangerous than the cliff.

952
01:02:44,300 --> 01:02:46,330
- Hey! Hee Ju... - Don't do anything...

953
01:02:46,800 --> 01:02:48,300
for my sake.
